# Hardware confirmed by esptool on 2026-09-24.
# On this ESP32-S3 rev. 0.2, the full OnStepX image watchdog-resets inside
# esp_wifi_init() when OPI PSRAM is enabled. OnStepX fits comfortably in
# internal RAM, so keep PSRAM disabled to allow Wi-Fi and avoid that conflict.
ONSTEPX_FQBN='esp32:esp32:esp32s3:USBMode=hwcdc,CDCOnBoot=cdc,UploadMode=default,CPUFreq=240,FlashMode=dio,FlashSize=16M,PartitionScheme=app3M_fat9M_16MB,PSRAM=disabled'
